# Sultan Beverages (مشروبات السلطان) - Cursor Rules & Core Principles

## CORE PRIORITIES
- PERFORMANCE, UNCOMPROMISING QUALITY, RIGOROUS SECURITY, AND CLEAN CODE ARE THE TOP PRIORITIES IN THIS PROJECT.
- Every piece of code generated must be production-ready, fully typed, optimized for quick execution, secure against unauthorized access, and structured following clean architecture guidelines.

---

## 1. Project Architecture & Code Standards
- Tech Stack: Vue 3 (Composition API using <script setup lang="ts">), Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, and Supabase.
- Modular Organization:
  - src/components/ui/ -> Atomic, highly reusable presentation elements.
  - src/components/layout/ -> Core shell structure (AppHeader, AppSidebar, MainLayout).
  - src/views/ -> Route-level views (POS, Inventory, Purchases, Suppliers, Reports, Auth).
  - src/stores/ -> Pinia modules for state management.
  - src/composables/ -> Isolated, testable logic for Supabase API interactions and network status.
  - src/types/ -> Explicit TypeScript declarations and Supabase generated schema types.
- TypeScript Enforcement:
  - Strict mode enabled (noImplicitAny, strictNullChecks).
  - NO any type usage under any condition. Define clean interfaces or type unions.

---

## 2. Design System & Apple Human Interface Guidelines
- Visual Identity: Clean Light Mode with Apple-inspired minimalist aesthetic.
- Primary Brand Palette: Burgundy / Deep Wine #800020 (configured cleanly across Tailwind shades 50 to 900).
- Aesthetics:
  - Subtle borders (border-slate-200/70), soft dynamic drop shadows (shadow-sm), and backdrop blur (backdrop-blur-md).
  - Ample padding, crisp typography hierarchy, clear focus indicators, and smooth state transitions.
  - ZERO "AI-style clichés": Do NOT generate neon gradients, saturated floating circles, or unnatural bright glow effects.

---

## 3. Database Architecture & Versioning (Supabase & PostgreSQL)
- Version-Controlled Migrations:
  - ALL database changes must strictly reside in supabase/migrations/ as numbered SQL scripts (e.g., 00001_initial_schema.sql).
  - NEVER alter, create, or drop tables/columns inside frontend application code.
- Row Level Security (RLS) & Security Protocols:
  - RLS MUST be explicitly enabled on every table.
  - Granular access policies must enforce role boundaries: admin retains full permissions; cashier holds restricted read/write access necessary solely for POS terminal operation.
  - All database queries must run through Supabase client TypeScript definitions.

---

## 4. Performance & Offline-First Engineering
- Offline Resiliency:
  - Intercept sales transactions when navigator.onLine === false.
  - Queue pending transactions locally via IndexedDB (Dexie.js) or Pinia local storage persistence.
  - Auto-sync queued transactions to Supabase sequentially upon network restoration with clear timestamping.
- UI/UX Optimization:
  - Minimize unnecessary component re-renders.
  - Implement debounced user input handlers for searching and barcoding.
  - Lazy-load views and heavy components via Vue Router dynamic imports.

---

## 5. Security & Error Handling
- Never expose sensitive service keys or private configuration in client code.
- Wrap all async Supabase API calls in clean try/catch blocks with explicit error logging and user-friendly toast notifications.
- Input Validation: Sanitize and validate all user inputs (forms, prices, quantities) before dispatching mutations.